course: dictionary
lesson: 3151
title: Emblems and what they stand for
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An emblem is a picture or object that stands for something bigger, such as a country, a team or an idea. When you see a maple leaf, you think of Canada. The picture is a sign that tells you something without any words.
explain: Use the words around a word to work out its meaning. «Ashoka's lion pillar is today a national emblem of India.» The word national tells you the lion is for the whole country, and the words emblem of India tell you it stands for India.
explain: An emblem can also show a quality, like peace. A dove is an emblem of peace, so when you see a dove, you think of calm and kindness. An emblem can also be a badge, like the school emblem on a uniform.
fact: An emblem is a picture or object that stands for a country, group, team or idea.
fact: «The maple leaf is the emblem of Canada.»
fact: A dove is an emblem of peace, so it stands for peace.
fact: Countries have national emblems, such as the rose of England, the thistle of Scotland and the kangaroo of Australia.
fact: An emblem can also be a badge with a picture on it, like a school emblem on a uniform.
exercise: What is an emblem? | A kind of weather that comes in winter | A loud noise made by a machine | *A picture or object that stands for a country, group or idea | A type of food eaten at breakfast
exercise: «The dove is an emblem of peace.» What does the dove stand for? | *Peace | Water | Speed | Winter
exercise: Which country does the maple leaf stand for? | *Canada | Australia | Scotland | Ireland
test: In «Ashoka's lion pillar is today a national emblem of India», which word tells you the emblem is for the whole country? | *national | lion | pillar | today
test: Which emblem stands for Scotland? | silver fern | *thistle | shamrock | kangaroo
exam: Which sentence uses emblem correctly? | *The bald eagle is an emblem of the USA | The rain fell all afternoon | The cat sat quietly on the mat | I went to the shop for milk
